  "title": "UseVisit Usage in Patient Chart",
  "updatedAt": 1793523226333,
  "answers": [
    {
      "id": "jPBPCKBHl9mtURRV",
      "productId": "openmrs",
      "question": "If `useVisit` in the OpenMRS frontend framework (openmrs-esm-core) changed its behaviour, which code in the patient chart app (openmrs-esm-patient-chart) uses it and could be affected?",
      "generation": "g-b59a21",
      "kind": "partial",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "## What is changing",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "`useVisit` lives in the framework package [1]. Its public contract is the `VisitReturnType` interface [2]: `error`, `mutate`, `isValidating`, `activeVisit`, `currentVisit`, `currentVisitIsRetrospective`, `isLoading`. It also drives the global visit-context store via `useVisitContextStore` [3], and returns `null` for the active visit when no visit has `stopDatetime === null` [4]. Any change to those fields, to the SWR cache keys it uses, or to when it writes visit context, shows up in the places below.",
          "citations": [
            1,
            2,
            3,
            4
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "## Confirmed consumers in openmrs-esm-patient-chart",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Depends on `activeVisit` only (rendering / menu entries):**\n- Patient banner \"Active Visit\" tag: renders only when `activeVisit` is truthy and `isLoading` is false [5]; it also reads `visitType.display` and `startDatetime` off the returned visit [6].\n- Visit attribute tags in the banner, which read `activeVisit.attributes` [7].\n- \"End active visit\" action button, shown only when `activeVisit` is set [8].\n- \"Delete active visit\" action button, which also passes the visit object into the delete dialog [9].",
          "citations": [
            5,
            6,
            7,
            8,
            9
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Depends on `activeVisit` + `mutate` (writes back to the cache):**\n- End-visit dialog calls `mutate()` after `updateVisit` succeeds, then clears the chart store's visit context if it matched [10]. If the behaviour of the returned `mutate` changes (e.g. it no longer revalidates the same SWR keys), this dialog's refresh path breaks.\n- Visit form workspace takes only `mutate` and calls it in `onVisitStarted` before handing the new visit to the store [11].",
          "citations": [
            10,
            11
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Depends on `activeVisit` + `isLoading`:**\n- Exported visit form uses `activeVisit` plus `isLoading: isLoadingVisit` to compute the \"patient already has an active visit\" conflict warning [12]. Because it masks `isLoading` itself, a change to when `isLoading` is true changes whether the warning appears during loading packages/framework/esm-react-utils/src/useVisit.ts.",
          "citations": [
            12
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Depends on `activeVisit`, `isValidating` and `mutate` (chart bootstrapping — the most sensitive call site):**\n- `usePatientChartPatientAndVisit` calls `useVisit` with `null` when a valid visit context already exists, else with the patient id, and uses `activeVisit`, `isValidating` and `mutate` to launch the workspace group and seed the chart store packages/esm-patient-chart-app/src/patient-chart/patient-chart.resources.ts. It gates initialisation on `!isValidatingVisitContext && !isValidatingActiveVisit` packages/esm-patient-chart-app/src/patient-chart/patient-chart.resources.ts, and passes the returned `mutateActiveVisit` into the workspace group as `mutateVisitContext` packages/esm-patient-chart-app/src/patient-chart/patient-chart.resources.ts. A change to the \"pass `null` to disable\" convention, to `isValidating`, or to the visit-context auto-set behaviour would affect chart entry. Note that `isValidating` is the OR of the active and retrospective calls packages/framework/esm-react-utils/src/useVisit.ts.",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Indirect: assumes the SWR cache key shape `useVisit` produces.** These do not import the hook but match on its request URL (`/visit?patient=…&includeInactive=false`), so they break silently if the hook's URL/keys change:\n- `invalidateVisitHistory` deliberately excludes the current-visit key from invalidation packages/esm-patient-common-lib/src/visit/revalidation-utils.ts.\n- `invalidateCurrentVisit`, which *does* target that key packages/esm-patient-common-lib/src/visit/revalidation-utils.ts.\n- `useOptimisticVisitMutations`, whose regexes rewrite the `/visit?patient=…` list cache entries that back `activeVisit` packages/esm-patient-common-lib/src/visit/visit-mutations.ts.\n- The header comment in `revalidation-utils.ts` claims \"28+ components\" depend on this hook packages/esm-patient-common-lib/src/visit/revalidation-utils.ts — that is a comment, not a code reference; only the imports listed above actually use it.",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Test doubles that encode the contract:**\n- `visit-form.test.tsx` mocks the hook with `activeVisit` shapes packages/esm-patient-chart-app/src/visit/visit-form/visit-form.test.tsx.\n- `patient-chart.resources.test.ts` mocks a full return object including `currentVisit`/`currentVisitIsRetrospective` packages/esm-patient-chart-app/src/patient-chart/patient-chart.resources.test.ts.\n- `visit-tag.test.tsx` sets `activeVisit`, `currentVisit`, `currentVisitIsRetrospective`, `error`, `isLoading`, `isValidating`, `mutate` packages/esm-patient-banner-app/src/banner-tags/visit-tag.test.tsx.\n- `immunizations-detailed-summary.test.tsx` still mocks the deprecated `currentVisit` field packages/esm-patient-immunizations-app/src/immunizations/immunizations-detailed-summary.test.tsx, even though no production code in this repo reads `currentVisit` (only its translations and the differently-named `currentVisitSummary` route do).\n- Also mocked, with return shapes not fully inspected: `stop-visit.test.tsx`, `delete-visit.test.tsx`, `end-visit-dialog.test.tsx`, `visit-attribute-tags.test.tsx`, `vitals-header.test.tsx` packages/esm-patient-vitals-app/src/vitals-and-biometrics-header/vitals-header.test.tsx.",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Vendored default mock in the framework** (would need updating alongside the hook): the shared mock returns `error`, `mutate`, `isValidating: true`, `currentVisit`, `activeVisit`, `currentVisitIsRetrospective` but no `isLoading` packages/framework/esm-react-utils/mock.tsx, with a parallel Jest version packages/framework/esm-react-utils/mock-jest.tsx. Tests that spread the real mock could see `isLoading` become `undefined`, which reads as \"not loading\".",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "## Likely but unverified",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "- Anything that consumes `mutateVisitContext` handed down through the workspace group props packages/esm-patient-chart-app/src/patient-chart/patient-chart.resources.ts — that value is `useVisit().mutate`, so a change to `mutate` propagates to every workspace that calls it, but which workspaces call it was not traced here.\n- The dynamic extension registrations (`currentVisitSummary`, routes) packages/esm-patient-chart-app/src/index.ts are name-adjacent only and do not appear to call the hook.\n- Other repos in scope may also consume the hook (e.g. the dispensing, laboratory or cohort-builder apps built on this framework); only the patient chart repo was searched for references.",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "## Could not check",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "- Dynamic dispatch and runtime extension loading: extensions receive `patientUuid` through slots, so a component could call `useVisit` without a static import that `find_symbol_references` sees.\n- Non-patient-chart repos and the deprecated `currentVisit`/`currentVisitIsRetrospective` fields' external consumers.",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "```mermaid\n---\ntitle: useVisit consumers in the patient chart\n---\nflowchart TD\n  hook[\"useVisit hook in esm-react-utils\"] --> store[\"useVisitContextStore\"]\n  hook --> tag[\"Banner Active Visit tag\"]\n  hook --> attr[\"Visit attribute tags\"]\n  hook --> stop[\"End visit action button\"]\n  hook --> del[\"Delete visit action button\"]\n  hook --> enddlg[\"End-visit dialog mutate\"]\n  hook --> vform[\"Visit form mutate\"]\n  hook --> evform[\"Exported visit form isLoading\"]\n  hook --> pchart[\"usePatientChartPatientAndVisit\"]\n  pchart --> group[\"Workspace group props\"]\n  hook -.-> keys[\"SWR cache keys matched by revalidation-utils and visit-mutations\"]\n```",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "A quick summary of what breaks first if behaviour changes:",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "| If `useVisit` changes… | Affected |\n|---|---|\n| `activeVisit` null/selection rule | banner tag, attribute tags, stop/delete buttons, exported visit form conflict warning, chart bootstrap |\n| `isLoading` semantics | banner tag (hidden while loading), exported visit form warning |\n| `isValidating` semantics | chart bootstrap gating in `usePatientChartPatientAndVisit` |\n| `mutate` (what it revalidates) | end-visit dialog refresh, visit form `onVisitStarted`, workspace group `mutateVisitContext` |\n| request URL / SWR keys | `invalidateVisitHistory`, `invalidateCurrentVisit`, optimistic mutations in `visit-mutations.ts` |\n| visit-context auto-set/clear side effects | chart bootstrap and every `usePatientChartStore` consumer |",
          "citations": []
        }
      ],
